README

Under the Circle environment, I have added the preemptive task scheduling function defined by the μITRON specification to this sample project.
To use this preemptive task scheduling function in your project, the following steps are required:
    Copy the added folders: Copy the arch, include, and ssp folders as they are into your project.
    Implement the hook routines: Ensure that sta_ker() and _kernel_handler() are called properly as hook routines.
    Prepare task functions: Implement your own task functions that you wish to execute.

Behavior of This Sample Project
This sample mainly outputs logs driven by timers.
    Timer Interrupt: Outputs a log message every 1 second.
    Task 2: Outputs a log message every 1 second, displaying the value of a counter variable incremented by Task 3.
    Task 3: Outputs a log message every 0.5 seconds and increments the counter variable.

License Note
The newly added source files fall under the TOPPERS License.


First blink 5 times to show the image was loaded right. After initializing most things the timer interrupt is on and the delay loop will be calibrated. A kernel timer is started to elapse after 15 seconds. Furthermore a log message is generated on every second.

When the kernel timer elapses TimerHandler() is called where a "Prefetch Abort" is generated by jumping to an invalid address (execute never bit is set in the page table for it). Alternatively you can generate an "Undefined Instruction" exception. This is for demonstrating the exception handler.
